Vivarium is released under two licences.

1. Code: the MIT License, for the files under oaos2/, tests/, scripts/, examples/ and docker/, the Python
   files under data/ outside data/competition-9.2/example_runs/, and pyproject.toml and uv.lock.
2. Documentation, materials and data: the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
   (CC BY 4.0), for the files under docs/ and library/, the other files under data/ outside
   data/competition-9.2/example_runs/, and README.md, REPLICATION.md and CITATION.cff. The licence text is at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.

The task packs under library/tasks/ are evaluation materials for AI agents. Each carries a canary
file (CANARY.txt). Please keep the canary when you redistribute the materials, and do not include
them in model training data. This request is not a condition of either licence.

The example runs under data/competition-9.2/example_runs/ are under neither licence. Their content was generated
by AI models (named in each run's MODELS.md); they are made available for research and teaching under the terms of
use in data/competition-9.2/example_runs/README.md, which bar their use for model training in any form.

